From: Ivo Zivkov <izivkov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 02:52:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Voice: recognize 'light duration' as its own setting

Previously any phrase containing the word 'light' (including 'set
light duration to long') was caught by the generic auto-light
regex and misrouted to the 'auto light' toggle, which is gated on
hasAutoLight and unsupported on models like ABL-100 and F-B100.
Light Duration is a separate, universally-supported feature
(light.duration) and should not have been blocked.

- IntentParser: added a dedicated 'light duration' pattern that
  is checked before the generic auto-light pattern, parsing
  'short'/'long'.
- VoiceDispatcher: maps 'light duration' to the light.duration
  featureId (always supported) and converts the spoken
  short/long into the watch's actual duration value via
  watchInfo.shortLightDuration/longLightDuration, since valid
  values differ per model (e.g. 2s/4s vs 1.5s/5s).
- Updated voice help text.
---
 src/voice/IntentParser.ts    | 11 +++++++++++
 src/voice/VoiceDispatcher.ts | 21 +++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 28 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/voice/IntentParser.ts b/src/voice/IntentParser.ts
index bbad955..369645d 100644
--- a/src/voice/IntentParser.ts
+++ b/src/voice/IntentParser.ts
@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ export class IntentParser {
     ];
 
     private languagePattern = /(?:set|change)?\s*(?:the\s*)?language\s*(?:to)?\s*(english|spanish|french|german|italian|russian)/i;
+    private lightDurationPattern = /light\s*duration/i;
     private buttonTonePattern = /(turn (on|off)|enable|disable|change|set)\s*(?:the\s*)?(button sound|button tone|sound)\s*(?:to)?\s*(on|off)?/i;
     private settingsDefaultPattern = /(?:set|change|reset)?\s*(?:the\s*)?settings(?:\s*(?:to)?\s*defaults?)?/i;
 
@@ -127,6 +128,16 @@ export class IntentParser {
             return { type: VoiceCommandType.SET_SETTING, params: { name: "button tone", value: enabled.toString() } };
         }
 
+        if (this.lightDurationPattern.test(text)) {
+            const isLong = /long/i.test(text);
+            const isShort = /short/i.test(text);
+            // Matched "light duration" explicitly: never fall through to the
+            // generic auto-light toggle below, even if short/long wasn't given.
+            return isLong || isShort
+                ? { type: VoiceCommandType.SET_SETTING, params: { name: "light duration", value: isLong ? "long" : "short" } }
+                : null;
+        }
+
         if (/auto light|light/i.test(text)) {
             const enabled = !/off|disable|disabled/i.test(text);
             return { type: VoiceCommandType.SET_SETTING, params: { name: "auto light", value: enabled.toString() } };
